  "limitations": [
    "Functional automated evidence for the exact pre-merge Core commit and separately pinned component. Post-merge release qualification and human UAT remain D5.",
    "Standalone uses runit with a systemd host bootstrap/delegation unit; a non-systemd PID 1 host is not qualified.",
    "Native physical IME, rich clipboard, programmatic text, host workspace integration, audio, UDP, files and other browsers are not qualified by D1.",
    "No resource/performance improvement or long-soak claim; reconnect timing is a local observation only.",
    "The component was rebuilt from fresh verified source archives on a host with build dependencies already installed. Fresh apt-only bootstrap, publication supply chain and complete distribution qualification remain Issue #26.",
    "Missing/malformed identity and Origin were tested at the existing single-account trusted ingress boundary. D1 does not add a per-user ACL inside one selected UID.",
    "Supervisor-loss health was checked after Manager restart. This does not establish immediate supervisor-loss detection.",
    "User-home systemd sessions now require systemd 250+ for ExitType=cgroup; standalone retains its delegated cgroup contract.",
    "Prior-Core rollback requires stopping writers and restoring compatible state; it is not live X-server adoption across providers."
  ],
